  "platform_principle_effects": {
    "autonomous_effect": "A valid externally issued one-shot grant can advance one exact STAGING run without reopening a reusable activation switch; every other run fails closed.",
    "global_effect": "The reusable authorization protocol is provider-neutral while each PostgreSQL target remains operation-specific and bounded to STAGING.",
    "irreplaceable_value_effect": "Authorization state and replay history live in a KIDULTS-controlled durable ledger rather than a provider or mutable workflow variable.",
    "transparency_effect": "Every allowed provider-credential activation is bound to exact repository, workflow, SHA, run, attempt, fresh request nonce, ledger-authoritative expiry, operation, target digest, and durable transaction receipt."
